From 75273e5bb5ff5cfa23b6c87f11eb44ccccf20a19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: medium <medium@debian.debian>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:22:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] fix(bittorrent): keep a tracker's domain and take tracker
 requests by their parameters

An HTTP tracker request lost its Host, so destOverride and domain rules no
longer saw the tracker; ordinary URLs that only mentioned info_hash= and
peer_id= were taken as BitTorrent; and every 20- or 21-byte datagram made
the LSD sniffer wait for a second read. A tracker request is now bittorrent
with the HTTP Host as its domain, overridden as HTTP's is; it needs an
announce or scrape path and whole query parameters; and LSD turns down a
short datagram whose bytes differ from its request line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
